# Documentation maintenance

Canonical policy: [docs/documentation-policy.md](docs/documentation-policy.md).

## Non-negotiables

- Document what exists and is verified, not what was intended. Do not claim completion from UI, registry entries, unrun tests, or generated stubs alone.
- Every material change needs a documentation-impact assessment. Update all affected canonical pages in the same change as the code and tests.
- Capability matrix: [docs/status.md](docs/status.md). Do not present planned work as available.
- One canonical source per subject. Prefer links and summaries over duplicate wording. Never hand-edit generated docs (`docs/parity-checklist.md` ← `cargo xtask parity`).
- English technical docs only: architecture, APIs, configuration, install, test, maintenance. No marketing copy.

## Before reporting done

- Run applicable tests; name any that were not run.
- List documentation files you changed (or explain why none were needed).
- Disclose limitations and remaining work; separate implemented from proposed follow-up.
- Never invent test results, APIs, or compatibility guarantees.
